cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use nano16s, please cite it along with the underlying tools listed in the README."
title: "nano16s: Nanopore full-length 16S rRNA amplicon analysis for local computers"
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake workflow for taxonomic profiling of Oxford Nanopore full-length
  16S rRNA amplicon data. Runs on an ordinary laptop or workstation with a
  single install command and no container or cluster requirement. Includes a
  builder for an up-to-date Emu reference database from the current NCBI 16S
  RefSeq Targeted Loci collection.
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Li
    affiliation: Mississippi State University
license: MIT
type: software
version: 1.0.0
keywords:
  - nanopore
  - 16S rRNA
  - microbiome
  - amplicon sequencing
  - taxonomic profiling
  - Emu
  - Snakemake
